1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth. Fame. Power.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer.

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,757
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,140
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:52,597
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:58,457
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,897
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,657
Is only legendary?

20
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,117
Until someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,557
Through it all!

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,497
Through all the trouble and times!

23
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain!

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,380
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:30,540
So come aboard and bring along
All your hopes and dreams.

27
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,020
Together we will find everything
That we're looking for.

28
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you.

29
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,460
If you wanna be my friend?

30
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,860
We are, we are on a cruise!

31
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,740
We are.

32
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:57,237
I don't care how much of
a badass he used to be!

33
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,017
Now he's just a cook.

34
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:02,117
I wouldn't have to break a
sweat to kill this old fart.

35
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,400
I'll spare him, but you have to leave.

36
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,697
Please, don't make this any harder, Sanji!

37
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:09,937
Just leave!

38
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,600
Don't force me to kill both of you!

39
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:16,560
Run away!

40
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,980
Not a chance!

41
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:23,497
You look even dumber at gunpoint, old man!

42
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:27,417
What kind of example do you think
you're setting for All the other cooks?

43
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,597
I don't need a lecture
from a brat like you!

44
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,737
Would you stop calling me names?

45
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:36,297
Quit treating me like a kid!

46
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:37,637
This is crazy!

47
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:40,277
Sanji wouldn't abandon Zeff, now would he?

48
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,217
Dean!

49
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,597
Point that gun at me!

50
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,677
Hey!

51
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,097
But what if you die?

52
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:48,180
Shut up!

53
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,920
Sanji, why you?

54
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,700
Someone's eager to die.

55
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:56,904
Lucky for you, I'd be
more than happy to oblige.

56
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,440
Allow me.

57
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:03,467
It would be my pleasure to beat
you to a bloody lifeless pulp.

58
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,260
Absolutely natural, Pearl! Surprise!

59
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:11,290
Sanji!

60
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,540
Why didn't you dodge that?

61
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:18,279
Because if I did, that rat over
there would pull the trigger on Zeff.

62
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,240
Why are you doing this?

63
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:23,337
Just leave the restaurant
peacefully and no one gets hurt.

64
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:24,250
Please!

65
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:27,040
This restaurant is that old man's life.

66
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:34,180
I've already taken everything
else that man holds dear.

67
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,320
His power.

68
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,020
His dreams.

69
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,860
So while I'm around,

70
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:50,140
I'm not gonna let anything
else get taken from him!

71
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,440
Behind you!

72
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:56,810
Sanji!

73
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:03,020
The Hell Blue!

74
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:08,740
Yeah, it's out there somewhere, and all
that's even awesomer than they say it is!

75
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,597
stop being a doofus
that's just a fairy tale

76
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:22,317
for seafaring cooks don't
get me wrong we've all

77
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,437
had our little fantasies
about it but you gotta

78
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:28,177
remember that it's just
a dream a dream well I'm

79
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,437
gonna find the all-blue
then we'll see who's

80
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:33,997
dreaming that's quite the
quest good luck all right

81
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,897
there little man tell
me do you even know what

82
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:38,900
kind of place the all-blue
is yeah I do I'm not

83
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:43,860
The all-blue is a place for
fish from all four seas, Lou.

84
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:49,500
There's fish from East Blue, the West
Blue, the North Blue, and the South Blue.

85
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:53,702
To cooks who have taken to the
sea, it's an irresistible paradise!

86
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,720
I'll find it!

87
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:57,960
Oh, yeah!

88
00:04:58,460 --> 00:04:59,917
That place is a gold mine.

89
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,357
It's got fish and plants
from all over the world.

90
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,657
Any chef would jump at
the chance to cook there.

91
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:05,570
True.

92
00:05:05,653 --> 00:05:08,277
The cooks I know would risk
life and limb to find it.

93
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,190
Yeah.

94
00:05:09,273 --> 00:05:10,720
Well, if it were real.

95
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:15,097
You think a miracle sea like the
all-blue could actually exist?

96
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:16,297
Think about it, kid.

97
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:17,321
It's impossible.

98
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:21,757
I bet it's probably just a lie
told by some daydreaming cook.

99
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,797
Okay, enough with the silly stories.

100
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:26,527
Get out there and collect
some plates, Sanji.

101
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,220
Oh, man. What a waste.

102
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:33,997
They left behind plates and plates
full of this delicious crop.

103
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,517
This one's barely been touched.

104
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,797
It's pretty good stuff, too.

105
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,277
I thought they'd love it for sure.

106
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:40,777
If you ask me, the customers
these days are spoiled.

107
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:43,597
It's way gross to eat the
leftovers of strangers.

108
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:46,097
You should just let me
throw that stuff away.

109
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:50,177
That kind of talk proves you've got a
whole lot to learn, so listen up, Shorty.

110
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:53,477
If you choose life on the high
seas, you've got to be resourceful.

111
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,877
The ocean is a strange
and unpredictable place

112
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,548
where wasting food could
be a fatal mistake.

113
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:02,140
So why don't you have some, eh? No way!

114
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,140
Don't go, people!

115
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,000
Panicking won't help!

116
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,520
Pirates are here!

117
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:15,780
What?

118
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:17,480
Pirates?

119
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,400
That ship!

120
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:24,140
It's Redfoot Zap and the Cook Pirates!

121
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:29,640
They're back from the Grand Line!

122
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:45,840
I take it you're the infamous
pirate, Captain Redfoot Zeff.

123
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,800
So, what do you want?

124
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:49,540
Steal!

125
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,380
Steal everything!

126
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:54,280
Addison nails down!

127
00:06:58,160 --> 00:06:59,717
Those bastards!

128
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,360
I refuse to die at the
hands of those animals.

129
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:06,660
Oh, look at this!

130
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:08,857
Hey, killer.

131
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:11,937
If you're not careful, you might
just put someone's eye out with that.

132
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:12,957
He got me.

133
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,637
Look, I'm bleeding.

134
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,837
Shut up.

135
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:18,680
You mongrels better stay away from me.

136
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:20,730
Sanji.

137
00:07:20,813 --> 00:07:22,780
Stop it, you'll make them mad.

138
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,577
A bit young to have a death wish.

139
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:28,197
But that's no reason not to grab it.

140
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:32,809
All right, you jerks, if I'm dying here,
then I'm taking some of you with me!

141
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,250
Donkey!

142
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,040
Wow, good one.

143
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,680
Yeah, that was brutal.

144
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:54,240
I'm not gonna die.

145
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,120
Not here!

146
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:02,780
I've got to live so that
I can find the all blue!

147
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:08,600
He said the all blue!

148
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:10,080
Pretty ambitious!

149
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:13,220
That's a good one!

150
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,873
Captain, should we tell the
little tyke it doesn't exist?

151
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,380
He won't... Shut up!

152
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:31,880
I'm not going to draw my last
breath until I've seen the old blue.

153
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:35,080
Captain, I recommend we
withdraw immediately.

154
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,754
This storm is way bigger than expected.

155
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:40,262
All right, men, playtime's over.

156
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:43,485
Let's load up the treasure
and get out of here.

157
00:08:51,420 --> 00:09:04,610
Ah!

158
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,980
Ah! Damn brat!

159
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:14,940
Captain!

160
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:18,177
Why'd he risk his life for one measly kid?

161
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:21,840
Oh, my God!

162
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,120
The Brat finally wakes up.

163
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,277
You're lucky to be alive, you know.

164
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:06,460
Yeah, thanks.

165
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:10,000
Moving isn't a good idea.

166
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:13,317
You're still pretty banged
up from the beating, Yutub.

167
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,500
What about the ships? Who knows?

168
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:17,537
It was a terrible storm.

169
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:19,796
our ships were most likely destroyed.

170
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:21,977
It seems we're the only survivors.

171
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:24,457
Washed ashore on a desolate rock?

172
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:27,481
without so much as a coconut
tree to give us food.

173
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,257
Sure, there are fish in the sea,

174
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:32,957
but the rock has been
curved by the waves in such

175
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:35,477
a manner that we wouldn't
be able to climb back up?

176
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,795
if we ever went down.

177
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:38,220
Sad, isn't it?

178
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,540
This is all your fault, old man!

179
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,100
I hope you die!

180
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,777
You can whine all you want.

181
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:44,690
It won't help.

182
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:49,551
If nobody comes, we'll just dry up and
become two more skeletons in the sea.

183
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:51,290
Skeletons?

184
00:10:51,373 --> 00:10:52,203
Really?

185
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:55,220
That bag there, it's your share of it.

186
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,496
It's some of the food that washed up.

187
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,601
Should be about five days' worth.

188
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:05,317
It's not much, but it's
better than nothing.

189
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,920
If you ration it out, it'll last longer.

190
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:09,905
Or use your head when you eat.

191
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,767
Good thing we're both cooks.

192
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:13,960
Hey, wait!

193
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,017
Is that bag your share of the food?

194
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:19,380
You got way more than me, you fat old pig!

195
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,260
Of course I get more food.

196
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:27,400
I'm a grown man, so I need more
to survive than a runt like you.

197
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:31,331
You should be grateful that
I'm sharing any of it with you.

198
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:35,240
Don't expect any pity
from me, you little brat.

199
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:39,010
Bastard!

200
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:45,435
Get to the other side of this
rock and watch for ships.

201
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,157
Let me know as soon as you see one.

202
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:51,977
Until then, don't bother talking
to me or moving from your post.

203
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:53,589
That'll just waste energy.

204
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:55,020
We can't afford that.

205
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:56,410
Good luck.

206
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:58,320
Screw you, Gramps.

207
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:00,893
I'm not saying anything if I see a ship.

208
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,320
I'll be fine.

209
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:04,837
I have five whole days worth of food.

210
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:07,497
We'll definitely see a ship
or two before I run out.

211
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:08,520
I'm sure of it.

212
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:11,858
Just to be extra safe, I'll
divide it up for 20 days.

213
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,037
That's more than enough
time to get rescued.

214
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:18,760
I guess all I got to do
now is sit and wait easy.

215
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:20,857
I'll make it through this thing.

216
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,000
No problem

217
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,340
Didn't see a ship today

218
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,180
That's all right.

219
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,086
It'll only be a few more days

220
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,020
I don't want to die.

221
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,000
This is it.

222
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,480
One moldy piece of bread.

223
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:15,440
Oh, man, what a waste.

224
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:18,777
They left behind plates and plates
full of this delicious grub.

225
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:21,742
It's way gross to eat the
leftovers of strangers.

226
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,647
You should just let me
throw that stuff away.

227
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:27,280
So why don't you have some, eh?

228
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:29,360
No way!

229
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,980
My last piece of bread.

230
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:33,357
I wonder...

231
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:36,840
Is the geyser dead yet?

232
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,700
He's alive!

233
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,020
And he's still got food!

234
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,360
A lot of food!

235
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,960
So much!

236
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:55,520
There's so much left!

237
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:01,800
You've got to get that food!

238
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:06,817
It's not fair that he has so
much more than me besides.

239
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,380
This is all his fault

240
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:24,140
What are you doing here your brat are
you here because you saw a ship I?

241
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:30,400
I came over here to
steal your food, old man.

242
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:32,957
If you want to kill me for it, go ahead.

243
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:36,393
Soon enough, I'll starve so
it makes no difference to me.

244
00:15:57,220 --> 00:16:01,000
Didn't I tell you not to come
over here unless you saw a ship?

245
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:04,570
Why?

246
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:07,820
You said it's full.

247
00:16:08,060 --> 00:16:09,140
Strange, isn't it?

248
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:12,436
We have all this money, and
yet we're going to starve.

249
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:16,620
It's only treasure.

250
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,160
It's worthless.

251
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:27,460
Hey, what's going on here old man?

252
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:28,779
Where's your food?

253
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:30,802
You had to have eaten something!

254
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:31,837
Now where is it?

255
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,100
I'm talking to you!

256
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,240
Answer me!

257
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:47,060
What happened to your leg?

258
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:50,120
The food!

259
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,733
Did you give me all of the food you had?

260
00:16:54,580 --> 00:16:55,540
I did.

261
00:16:55,980 --> 00:17:00,627
And you had to have known that without
that leg, you'd never be a pirate again.

262
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:01,720
That's right.

263
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:04,020
You old fool!

264
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,700
Why'd you help me?

265
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,220
It doesn't make sense to
sacrifice so much for me!

266
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:12,917
So why?

267
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:13,960
Tell me!

268
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:20,100
Because for my entire life,
I've had the same dream as you.

269
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,540
Be all blue.

270
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:28,377
But your men said that it doesn't exist.

271
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,417
Of course it does.

272
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:31,957
Never mind them.

273
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:33,737
When the time comes.

274
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:35,237
Head to the Grand Line.

275
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:37,537
That's where the old blue is sure to be.

276
00:17:37,620 --> 00:17:39,037
My days.

277
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,040
As a pirate are done.

278
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,597
But you have your whole life.

279
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:44,580
To find it.

280
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:48,217
Don't die now. Get up.

281
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:49,840
Come on old man.

282
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,400
Don't you dare give up.

283
00:17:54,140 --> 00:18:00,500
I wonder how many men have lost
their lives cursing the ocean,

284
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:03,132
knowing that it will soon be their grave.

285
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:08,777
This isn't the first time I've been
hungry enough to look death in the eyes,

286
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:11,280
and my thoughts are the same each time.

287
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:16,960
It is always my deepest wish that there
be a restaurant in the middle of the sea.

288
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,150
A restaurant?

289
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,877
Yeah, I was thinking that if I
make it out of this mess alive,

290
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:25,780
I'd like to build a restaurant
as my final purpose in life.

291
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,310
Great!

292
00:18:27,393 --> 00:18:28,717
And I'll even help you do it!

293
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:29,980
So don't die, okay?

294
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:35,177
A weak little brat like you
couldn't be much good for anything.

295
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:36,672
Then I'll become strong!

296
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,940
So, don't die!

297
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:54,670
Help!

298
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:58,520
The geezer needs help! Over here!

299
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,580
Please help!

300
00:18:59,820 --> 00:19:02,160
Please, please help us!

301
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,000
Hey!

302
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,030
Hey!

303
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:10,960
Over here! Help us! This way!

304
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:12,080
Please, please!

305
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:16,800
Over here! Over here!
Help! Help! This way!

306
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:21,560
That old coot.

307
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:25,480
He gave up his legs so that I could live.

308
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:35,077
There's no way to repay the old geezer for

309
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:37,689
his kindness unless I
risk my life for him!

310
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:44,650
Why?

311
00:19:44,733 --> 00:19:46,440
Why are you standing, Sanji?

312
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,640
Stay down.

313
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:51,140
I'm afraid I can't do that.

314
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:53,595
It's a little too much like giving up.

315
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:56,310
Idiot!

316
00:19:56,393 --> 00:19:57,440
I'll kill you!

317
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:02,540
Cue little brat.

318
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:04,670
Ha!

319
00:20:04,753 --> 00:20:06,540
That is so very refined of you.

320
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:09,172
But this restaurant will be closing soon.

321
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,580
And it'll open again for business.

322
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,420
As a pirate ship.

323
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,400
No, don't!

324
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:19,100
Gino, shoot the old man!

325
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:21,040
What's it do?

326
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,380
No, don't, don't!

327
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:28,380
Battle of it!

328
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:49,457
In my mind That I knew would Leave me I

329
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:53,597
had to find my way To that place Before

330
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:57,777
someone could beat me The promised land

331
00:20:57,860 --> 00:21:02,400
Was in my grasp And I wouldn't let go

332
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,597
My only dream

333
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:12,297
I won't stop

334
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,520
chasing it Until it comes true

335
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:20,277
But if the world ever

336
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:24,397
changes I call out your name

337
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:30,660
We could return to the time
When everything's the same

338
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:36,997
As long as I'm with you My memories won't

339
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:43,040
fade Waiting for that one true dream?
